# ADR files always

When an operate design, integration Close, or architecture handoff records an
accepted (or human-approved) architectural decision:

1. **Write** a numbered ADR under `docs/adr/` (next free `NNNN-kebab-title.md`).
2. Do **not** leave the decision only as “proposed ADR text” inside
   `agent-system/design-*.md` or handoff YAML.
3. Use the next free number — never reuse an existing ADR id (e.g. ADR-0003 is
   already edit-canvas vs export preview).
4. Match existing ADR shape: Status, Context, Decision, Consequences; prefer
   `CONTEXT.md` vocabulary for CV terms.
5. Link the ADR from the design note / archive summary when those artifacts exist.
6. Do **not** silently overwrite prior ADRs; supersede explicitly if needed.
